\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Equal endpoints do not identify the reviewed instance. Candidate c1 proposes 100; grant a1 authorizes the correction 101 for c1. Candidate c2 retains the same context $K$ with a different identifier. Alternative paths start from state 90 with a1 unconsumed and all shared checks satisfied: context binding admits either candidate, whereas instance binding admits only c1. Diamonds are checks, capsules are states/transitions, and the stop bar means no commit. A matching new grant may authorize c2. The four roles are proposal 100, correction 101, reviewed c1 and executed transition $90\to 101$. Conceptual construction; AI-generated object glyphs are disclosed below}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:gap}{{1}{2}{Equal endpoints do not identify the reviewed instance. Candidate c1 proposes 100; grant a1 authorizes the correction 101 for c1. Candidate c2 retains the same context $K$ with a different identifier. Alternative paths start from state 90 with a1 unconsumed and all shared checks satisfied: context binding admits either candidate, whereas instance binding admits only c1. Diamonds are checks, capsules are states/transitions, and the stop bar means no commit. A matching new grant may authorize c2. The four roles are proposal 100, correction 101, reviewed c1 and executed transition $90\to 101$. Conceptual construction; AI-generated object glyphs are disclosed below}{figure.1}{}}
