\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Binding and recovery are separate design choices. Under shared checks and content-immutable candidate records, if the compared content fields \(R\) include the retained context fields \(K\), the admissible request sets satisfy \(A_{\mathrm  {instance}}\subseteq A_{\mathrm  {content}}\subseteq A_{\mathrm  {context}}\subseteq A_{\mathrm  {value}}\). These inclusions need not be strict; context and content binding coincide when \(K=R\). Following an instance-mismatch rejection, the system may offer reuse of the reviewed candidate under the existing authorization or obtain matching authorization for another candidate. Reauthorization is a recovery branch, not another binding level. Each continuation must pass a new admission check; the schematic does not guarantee that an available route will be taken. Object glyphs were AI-generated; see the AI-assisted preparation declaration}}{10}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:design}{{2}{10}{Binding and recovery are separate design choices. Under shared checks and content-immutable candidate records, if the compared content fields \(R\) include the retained context fields \(K\), the admissible request sets satisfy \(A_{\mathrm {instance}}\subseteq A_{\mathrm {content}}\subseteq A_{\mathrm {context}}\subseteq A_{\mathrm {value}}\). These inclusions need not be strict; context and content binding coincide when \(K=R\). Following an instance-mismatch rejection, the system may offer reuse of the reviewed candidate under the existing authorization or obtain matching authorization for another candidate. Reauthorization is a recovery branch, not another binding level. Each continuation must pass a new admission check; the schematic does not guarantee that an available route will be taken. Object glyphs were AI-generated; see the AI-assisted preparation declaration}{figure.2}{}}
